          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy dual fuel for the propane, and size it on the propane rating. For most houses, the Westinghouse WGen9500DF is the best balance of propane output, outlets and convenience, and the Champion 9200-Watt Dual Fuel with CO Shield is the value alternative with carbon monoxide shutoff built in.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Then spend as much attention on the rest of the plan as on the generator: a properly installed transfer switch or interlock, enough propane cylinders for the outage you expect, a spot at least 20 feet from the house, and working CO alarms inside. That is what turns a generator in the shed into power when the grid goes down.
          </p>
